' The stage set for the VBCCR18 section: the control instances its samples assume.
'
' A sample on a control's page says `ProgressBar1.Value = 50`, which is form code-behind:
' the reader has a form with the control on it, named by the designer. This template has a
' form for each control of the package, frm<Class>, with that one control on it, and each
' property here loads the control's form and returns the control, so that a sample that is
' run works on a real control. The Load is explicit, as contributed-VBFLXGRD18's is. A sample
' that names two controls gets them from two forms.
'
' A type is written `VBCCR18.<Class>`, the project's name and then the class's: several of
' the classes have the names of controls of other packages (ListView, ProgressBar).

Module tbxStageVBCCR18

    Public Property Get Animation1() As VBCCR18.Animation
        Load frmAnimation
        Return frmAnimation.Animation1
    End Property

    Public Property Get CheckBoxW1() As VBCCR18.CheckBoxW
        Load frmCheckBoxW
        Return frmCheckBoxW.CheckBoxW1
    End Property

